  "summary": "Founded and led the video search team for 5 years at Google starting in early 2006 (pre youtube acquisition) Crawling, transcoding, thumb-nailing, meta data extraction, categorical classification, indexing and serving of search results. 10,000 QPS 24/7 highly available service, exabytes of data storage. By 2011 our results were merged into the main Google search engine and were responsible for 7% of overall impressions. \n\nLed the engineering and camera subsystems power design for the Cassini program at JPL. 1991-1993\n\nFundamental color vision research with the founder of Tandent Vision Science. \n\nFundamental research of the physical implementation of analog neural network-type signal processors. See Phd related publications.",
